      'about_detail':
          'JA MES Tool v2.9.0\n\nAutomated tool for fetching, inspecting, and exporting product test records, process/barcode history, and BOM component traceability from the Foxconn CloudMES system.\n\nKey Features:\n• Command Palette (Ctrl+K / Cmd+K): a spotlight-style search over every tab, action, and setting — type to filter, arrow keys + Enter or click to run\n• Bento Glassmorphism Architecture: Modern layout inspired by Apple Liquid Glass, Bento Grid, Dynamic Island, and GPU-composited drifting Mesh Orbs\n• Four Data Views: Test Record, Barcode History & Component List per SN, plus Component Trace — a reverse lookup from a component\'s own CSN to the product SN it\'s installed into\n• Live-Preview 4-Slider Glassmorphism Controls: Real-time interactive sliders for Card Blur (0-40px), Card Opacity (5-100%), Dialog Blur (0-40px), and Dialog Opacity (10-100%) in Advanced Settings, with instant UI updates, Default reset, and Cancel rollback\n• 1-Click Direct Theme Switcher: Instant seamless toggle between Light and Dark mode\n• Precise Automatic Build Timestamping: Automatically extracts accurate compilation date/time from compiled data/app.so and executable, displayed in Header & About\n• Component Trace keeps its own persisted search history in the sidebar, sharing the SN queue\'s add/search box (behavior switches automatically by active tab), with matching Search/Sort and CSV Template/Import/Export\n• Automatic SN Master Resolution: internal SNs auto-resolve to the canonical product SN, shown as "typed SN → resolved SN" (auto-scrolling when it doesn\'t fit) plus a "Next" chip for the SN\'s next process\n• iOS-style Smooth UI Transitions: animated tab/SN switching, cascading list entrance, scale+fade dialogs, and crossfaded theme switching\n• Excel-style Search Filter & Sort-by on every record list, with a frosted-glass Sort dropdown using real BackdropFilter blur\n• Selectable & Copyable record data, including the SN queue sidebar (click-drag / double-click + Ctrl+C)\n• Per-SN & Refresh-All Buttons: re-fetch any SN or the whole queue on demand without restarting the app\n• Dynamic-Island Hover Toolbar (compact icons, full labels on hover/maximize)\n• Automated SN Queue & Parallel Record Fetching\n• Automatic Startup Expired Token Warning Popup\n• Edge & Chrome Multi-Browser Compatibility (Anti-Freeze Flags)\n• Persistent browser-specific Chrome and Edge profiles preserve sessions, passwords, and bookmarks across restarts\n• Bounded CDP readiness checks and launch de-duplication prevent browser startup hangs\n• Verified Connection Badge Icon 🛡️ in Settings\n• Automatic SN Queue Refetch on Settings Save\n• Smart CSV Import (auto-skips header rows like "SN") & Export\n• Automatic CDP Credential Interception (Token, UUID, Cookie)\n• Smart 2-Step Auto Sync Wizard\n• Collapsible & Expandable Advanced Settings\n• Automatic Token Verification every 3 minutes\n• Header Sanitization (fixes Carriage Return \\r\\n & quote errors)\n• System Logs auto-cleared after 7 days\n• Multi-language Support (English, Vietnamese, Chinese)\n• Modern Glassmorphic Light/Dark UI Theme',
      'user_guide_detail':
          '📖 USER GUIDE (v2.9.0)\n\n1. Command Palette (Ctrl+K / Cmd+K):\n   - Press Ctrl+K (or Cmd+K on macOS keyboards) anywhere in the app to open a spotlight-style search over every tab, action, and setting.\n   - Type to filter by name or keyword, use ↑/↓ to highlight a result, and press Enter or click to run it. Press Esc or click outside to close.\n\n2. Add Serial Numbers (SN):\n   - Manual: Type SN into the left sidebar input box and press [+] or Enter. If you type an internal/alias SN, it is automatically resolved to the canonical product SN before fetching — the header shows "typed SN → resolved SN" (scrolling automatically if the label doesn\'t fit), plus a "Next" chip when the SN\'s next process is known.\n   - CSV Batch: Click [Template] to download the sample CSV file. Fill in your SNs, then click [Import]. The app automatically skips title headers containing "SN".\n   - SN text in the queue can be selected (click-drag) and copied with Ctrl+C. Each SN has its own refresh icon to re-fetch just that SN, and the header has a [Refresh All] button to re-fetch the whole queue — no need to restart the app.\n\n3. Three Data Views per SN:\n   - Hover the icon toolbar near "Result Details" to reveal its label, or just click it: [Test Record] pass/fail test results, [Barcode History] full process/station routing, [Component List] WIP BOM / material traceability.\n   - Each list has a search box (matches any field) and a [Sort] button — click a field to sort, click again to flip ascending/descending.\n   - Record text can be selected and copied directly with the mouse.\n   - Click [Export] to save all fetched Test Record data to a structured CSV file.\n\n4. Component Trace (reverse component lookup):\n   - Click the [Component Trace] tab — the sidebar switches from the SN queue to a Trace History list, and the same input box now searches component CSNs instead of adding SNs.\n   - Type or scan a component\'s CSN and press [+]/Enter — paste multiple CSNs at once (one per line, or comma-separated) to search them all in one go.\n   - Each searched CSN becomes a row in the Trace History sidebar (click to revisit a cached result, refresh icon to re-run it, X to remove it) and is saved to disk, so the history survives closing and reopening the app.\n   - The result panel shows every product SN the CSN is currently installed into, with the same search/sort toolbar as the other 3 views. [Template]/[Import]/[Export] automatically operate on CSNs while this tab is active.\n\n5. Auto Token & Credential Sync (Browser CDP):\n   - Open Settings ⚙️ or use the Automatic Startup Expired Token Warning Popup.\n   - Step 1: Click [1. Open Browser] to launch Chrome or Edge. The app reuses separate persistent profiles for each browser, so saved sessions, passwords, and bookmarks remain available.\n   - Log into your MES account on the web page.\n   - Step 2: Click [2. Sync Credentials]. The app uses CDP Network Interception to capture live Token, UUID, Operation-ID & Cookie.\n   - Alternatively, expand Advanced Settings and click [Paste Raw Header (Postman)] to paste Postman raw requests.\n   - Saving Settings automatically clears old errors and re-fetches the entire SN queue and Component Trace history.\n\n6. Advanced Configuration:\n   - Click [Expand Advanced Settings ▼] to manually edit Token, Cookie, Operation-ID, UUID, or Language.\n   - Open the "Glassmorphism" → [Customize blur & transparency] section to adjust Main Background Blur/Opacity and Dialog Blur/Opacity with a live preview as you drag each slider. Click [Default] to restore all 4 to their factory values.\n\n7. Connection Health Check:\n   - Status indicator near "Settings" title shows Green (Connected) or Amber (Check Status).\n   - Tokens are validated automatically every 3 minutes.\n   - Click the verify 🛡️ icon in Settings to test connection manually — it animates into a green check or red cross for a few seconds to show the result, and its tooltip shows the detailed message.\n\n8. Logs & Maintenance:\n   - Logs are saved daily in the "logs" folder next to the .exe file.\n   - Log files older than 7 days are automatically cleaned up on app launch.',
